gnostic on the BLOCKED branch (gh-757 review): a guest PR's kicker-masked head is equally stranded, and validating external PRs is the sanctioned prerequisite for the external review flow — only the auto-REWORK arm is machine-gated, never the validation dispatch. Runs immediately AFTER validate-fresh, same dev-lane pacing (limit 1, no mutex — the merge window's mutexAmong [pr_approved] is untouched). Green verdicts flow through validated-green exactly as validate-fresh's do; red verdicts converge through sweep-stale-validating (which probes the dispatched run, not the masked rollup) into the standard fail path. gh-829 CLEAN ARM (live 2026-10-10: PR #826 — issue gh-825 latch ai_developed present, head all-green, CLEAN, ZERO labels for hours, no ai_validating, no review, nothing; the CLEAN exclusion assumed merge-validated owns CLEAN, but merge-validated needs pr_approved, which a zero-label PR can never reach without first being validated — the dead-zone family missed the CLEAN case): the CLEAN exclusion now narrows to a mergeStateLatch instead of dropping — green + CLEAN + zero lifecycle labels + the PR's linked issue carrying ai_developed (the dev leg's done-marker latch — machine-work gating: a guest/unlinked PR without the latch stays excluded exactly as before, AC3) → the same probe-dispatch-arm flow arms validation in one tick (AC1); ANY lifecycle label keeps the PR untouched (AC2 — notLabels disjointness stands, all existing rules keep their lanes). The latch guard fails CLOSED (no linked issue or fetch failure = excluded, never matched) and reads the linked issue's labels through the per-tick TTL cache — no extra API pressure per rule pass.",
