  "localAction": "validate_pr",
  "limit": 1,
  "id": "validate-fresh"
},        {
  "description": "Post-dev dead-zone fix (gh-759, live fa 2026-10-06: PRs #1305/#1306/#1309/#1311/#1312 — five fresh machine PRs BLOCKED with ZERO labels for hours, each unblocked by hand-arming ai_validating + dispatching CI; agents #756 / fa #1295 / fa #1304 are the same class patched by hand the same day). The dev leg completes (issue ai_developed + status:In Review) and the fresh head IMMEDIATELY carries GREEN check runs from the deployment's ambient workflows (fa: kicker sm-liveness/head-completeness, CodeQL, the analyze suite) — while the DISPATCH-ONLY validation CI (jobParams.ciWorkflow, no push trigger) has never been ordered. The rollup reads 'green', so validate-fresh (checks [none, pending]) never matches; every verdict/re-dispatch rule needs ai_validating or pr_approved, and the PR carries zero labels — nothing ever arms validation and the PR dead-locks. This rule is the UN-ARMED twin of revalidate-armed-green (gh-922): rollup green + none of ai_validating/pr_approved/chore:pin/validation_failed → validate_pr probes the head for a dispatched CI run — none (or cancelled-only) → dispatch + arm ai_validating; a completed GREEN run → skipIfGreenCi skips (the blocker is another workflow's required check — re-running loops forever). gh-850 LATCH VOID (live fa #1457 2026-10-11 05:0x, per-head-sha invariant): ai_validated no longer excludes the PR here either — a latched PR whose head moved onto an ambient-green but CI-absent sha is exactly the gh-850 deadlock shape (the old green run covers the OLD head, not this one): the action's head-scoped cover probe finds no green ON THIS HEAD → the stale latch is stripped and validation re-dispatches; a green dispatched run covering the current head keeps the skipIfGreenCi dead-zone skip untouched (AC2). Disjoint from validate-fresh by construction (none/pending vs green) and from every verdict rule by labels; notMergeState excludes BEHIND (silent-update refreshes first) and DIRTY (conflict-rework). Deliberately author-agnostic on the BLOCKED branch (gh-757 review): a guest PR's kicker-masked head is equally stranded, and validating external PRs is the sanctioned prerequisite for the external review flow — only the auto-REWORK arm is machine-gated, never the validation dispatch. Runs immediately AFTER validate-fresh, same dev-lane pacing (limit 1, no mutex — the merge window's mutexAmong [pr_approved] is untouched). Green verdicts flow through validated-green exactly as validate-fresh's do; red verdicts converge through sweep-stale-validating (which probes the dispatched run, not the masked rollup) into the standard fail path. gh-829 CLEAN ARM (live 2026-10-10: PR #826 — issue gh-825 latch ai_developed present, head all-green, CLEAN, ZERO labels for hours, no ai_validating, no review, nothing; the CLEAN exclusion assumed merge-validated owns CLEAN, but merge-validated needs pr_approved, which a zero-label PR can never reach without first being validated — the dead-zone family missed the CLEAN case): the CLEAN exclusion now narrows to a mergeStateLatch instead of dropping — green + CLEAN + zero lifecycle labels + the PR's linked issue carrying ai_developed (the dev leg's done-marker latch — machine-work gating: a guest/unlinked PR without the latch stays excluded exactly as before, AC3) → the same probe-dispatch-arm flow arms validation in one tick (AC1); ANY lifecycle label keeps the PR untouched (AC2 — notLabels disjointness stands, all existing rules keep their lanes). The latch guard fails CLOSED (no linked issue or fetch failure = excluded, never matched) and reads the linked issue's labels through the per-tick TTL cache — no extra API pressure per rule pass.",
  "source": "github",
  "query": {

