{"newText":"    test('no previous snapshot — fresh carry; garbage prev tolerated', function () {
        var cary = mod.mergeDeadZoneCary(null, { blocked: [{ prNumber: 7 }], scannedAt: '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z' });
        assert.equal(cary.blockedAt['7'], '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z');
        assert.equal(mod.mergeDeadZoneCary({ blocked: 'garbage' }, null).blocked.length, 0);
    });

    test('every degraded shape degrades to a fresh carry, never a crash', function () {
        // blockedAt of the wrong type is not trusted — stamps start over.
        var cary = mod.mergeDeadZoneCary(
            { blockedAt: 'garbage' },
            { blocked: [{ prNumber: 9 }], scannedAt: '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z' });
        assert.equal(cary.blockedAt['9'], '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z');
        // No scannedAt on the current scan — the carry stamps now itself.
        var unstamped = mod.mergeDeadZoneCary(null, { blocked: [{ prNumber: 10 }] });
        assert.equal(typeof unstamped.blockedAt['10'], 'string', 'stamped with the scan time');
        assert.ok(unstamped.blockedAt['10'].indexOf('T') !== -1, 'an ISO timestamp');
        // Malformed entries drop out; the readable ones stay.
        var mixed = mod.mergeDeadZoneCary(null, {
            blocked: [null, {}, { prNumber: 11 }], scannedAt: '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z'
        });
        assert.equal(mixed.blocked.length, 1);
        assert.equal(mixed.blockedAt['11'], '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z');
    });","oldText":"    test('no previous snapshot — fresh carry; garbage prev tolerated', function () {
        var cary = mod.mergeDeadZoneCary(null, { blocked: [{ prNumber: 7 }], scannedAt: '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z' });
        assert.equal(cary.blockedAt['7'], '2026-10-19T23:00:00Z');
        assert.equal(mod.mergeDeadZoneCary({ blocked: 'garbage' }, null).blocked.length, 0);
    });","path":"js/unit-tests/test_guestValidationPath.js"}

3 failures. My refactor broke semantics. Let me analyze:

Test: 'real red verdict (FAILURE, TIMED_OUT) reddens the tally' expects real=3, red=2. Got real=4?? 

The inputs: SUCCESS, FAILURE, TIMED_OUT. Original semantics: real++ for non-bokeping non-canceled → 3. Mine: bucket !== 'bokept' && bucket !== 'canceled' → real++ → 3 red... wait got real 4? Let me re-check my code:

```js
for (var i = 0; i < checkRuns.length; i++) {
   var bucket = _tallyBucket(_normalizeRun(checkRuns[i]), bokepingPrefixes);
   if (bucket !== 'bokept' && bucket !== 'canceled') t.real++;
   t[bucket]++;
}
``

Hmm — `t[bucket]++` with bucket='real' increments t.real... and real++ ALSO incremented. For a 'real' (green) bucket: real++ then t.real++ → +2! Bug! Original: real++ once per run. For 'red' bucket: real++ and t.red++ ✓. For 'pending': real++ and t.pending++ ✓. But for green 'real': real++ + t['real']++ = double increment!

Fix: only do the extra real++ for red/pending, or increment once:
```js
if (bucket === 'red' || bucket === 'pending') t.real++;
t[bucket]++;
``
Wait no — real must count red + pending + green. t.red/t.pending/t.real are separate counters. Original increments real for EVERY non-bokeping non-canceled run and red/pending ADDITIONALLY. So:
- green: t.real++ only → bucket 'real' → t[bucket]++ → t.real++ ✓ (no extra).
- red: t.real++ AND t.red++ → bucket 'red' → t[bucket]++ gives red++, need extra real++.
- pending: t.real++ AND t.pending++ → extra real++ needed.

So: `if (bucket === 'red' || bucket === 'pending') t.real++; t[bucket]++;` — correct and CC-cheap.

Third failure: 'empty rollup — zero real checks'? It said passed 22 failed 3 — third failure not shown in tail. Let me see all failures.

